messages:
incident-bot: 🔔 [PAGER] Critical: rapid increase in 5xx errors from inference-prod-us-west. 5xx rate > 3% sustained for 12m. Several customer requests failing. Paging on-call.

sara: On call — taking lead. Thanks. Any obvious recent deploys?

miguel: I don't see a deploy in the last 30m. Autoscaler bumped capacity earlier but no infra changes.

alice: I'm seeing spike aligns with higher long-context generation jobs (seq len > 4096). KV cache misses up.

sara: ok. Immediate mitigation plan: 1) soft-rate-limit free/anonymous tier 2) reduce max_tokens default for public endpoints 3) enable 429 backpressure at edge. Who can flip the rate-limit?

dry: (note: dry-run name used for illustration)

ryan: I can push a temporary rate clamp on the edge shaper. Will set per-API-key limits for anonymous and trial customers to 40r/s total.

mike: I'll prepare a quota clamp to limit token throughput via admin.

alice: Also suggest disabling streaming for high-context models as a temporary feature gate — reduces KV churn.

sara: good call. Miguel, can you confirm which customers are impacted and surface to support?

miguel: Early list: customer-a (heavy embeddings), partner-b (chat history replays). Impact: intermittent 500s, retries from their SDKs are spiking.

support-ops: Notified CS. Drafting a message to affected customers (will include recommended client-side retry guidance).

sara: Execute mitigations in this order: (A) admin quota clamp, (B) edge rate-limit soft clamp, (C) disable streaming for heavy models, (D) monitor. Only step back if errors drop.

ryan: Applying edge soft-rate-limit now. Command (internal):

```
# Set soft rate limit via edge API
curl -X POST "https://edge-api.internal/redwood/ratelimit" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ADMIN_TOKEN" \
  -d '{"scope":"anonymous","rate":40,"burst":80,"mode":"soft"}'
```

ryan: Patch applied. Watching metrics.

mike: Applying quota clamp in admin console for free-tier -> tokens/min = 12000. Using UI, but here's API for audit: 

```
POST /admin/v1/quotas/tenants/free-tier
{
  "token_rate_per_minute": 12000,
  "note": "temporary clamp due to 5xx surge"
}
```

mike: Quota change done. Audit ID: q-238765.

alice: Disabling streaming for large-model group now. Deploy-bot, can you gate the feature flag?

deploy-bot: feature-flag updated: streaming.large-models = false (cfg-change-id: ff-8723). Rolling out to us-west.

alice: Observability: KV-cache miss rate reduced by ~15% after gating. 5xx rate trending down but still elevated (1.2%).

sara: Good. Next: client/SDK guidance to reduce retry thundering and avoid duplication. Drafted guidance below. Support, add to customer message.

alice: SDK guidance (short):
- Use idempotency keys for all non-idempotent requests (create/submit flows). Name key: `idempotency_key` header.
- Implement exponential backoff with full jitter. Start at 200ms, max 10s, max retries 5.
- On 429 prefer retry-after header; on 5xx use backoff.
- Avoid immediate burst retries from concurrent threads — add per-process token bucket.

sara: Put that in code snippets.

alice: Code example (JS):

```
// pseudo-SDK retry wrapper
async function requestWithRetries(opts) {
  let attempt = 0;
  const base = 200; // ms
  while (attempt < 5) {
    try {
      return await sdk.request(opts);
    } catch (err) {
      attempt++;
      if (err.status === 429 && err.headers['retry-after']) {
        await sleep(Number(err.headers['retry-after']) * 1000);
      } else if (is5xx(err)) {
        const jitter = Math.random() * (base * Math.pow(2, attempt));
        const wait = Math.min(10000, base * Math.pow(2, attempt)) + jitter;
        await sleep(wait);
      } else {
        throw err;
      }
    }
  }
  throw new Error('max-retries-exceeded');
}

// ensure you set an idempotency header for non-idempotent ops
await sdk.request({path:'/v1/generate', headers:{'Idempotency-Key': uuid()}});
```

alice: Also recommend client-side concurrency limits: cap in-flight requests per process to 8 for high-latency endpoints.

sara: Add example for curl/curl users showing idempotency header.

alice: Curl snippet: 

```
curl https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" \
  -H "Idempotency-Key: ${UUID}" \
  -d '{"model":"rwd-llama-large","prompt":"..."}'
```

miguel: For SDK maintainers: we should ship a tiny update to default retry policy to include jitter and limit concurrent retries, but avoid forcing consumers; mark as advisory and ship in next patch.

mike: Post-mitigation: errors down to 0.4% across region. Close monitoring for 60m. Recommend rolling back streaming flag only after 90m stable.

support-ops: Sent customer notifications with the suggested client guidance and mitigation summary.

sara: Thanks team. Follow-up actions (assignments):
- miguel: produce customer impact list and export logs (action: export-238765)
- alice: prepare SDK advisory PR with retry examples (PR ready in 2h)
- ryan: revert edge soft-limit only if stable for 90m (monitor runbook)
- mike: include quota clamp audit ID in postmortem notes

sara: I'll mark this thread as active incident. If we see regression, escalate to infra-signal.

incident-bot: Incident created: INC-238765. Severity: P2 -> monitoring for 60m.

mike: Adding postmortem stub in /incidents/inc-238765. Will fill in mitigation timeline.

alice: One more client note: recommend adding `Idempotency-Key` into SDK request builder to make it opt-out. That will reduce duplicates in failover situations.

sara: Great. Closing live mitigation window for now — team continue monitoring, update thread with any regression. :thumbsup:
